---
title: White Sandwich Bread
description: Two sandwich loaves from an instant-yeast dough that swaps the first rise for a 10-minute rest.
tags: [bread, baking]
course: side
icons: [wheat, sandwich, oven]
source:
  name: Crazy for Crust
  author: Dorothy Kern
  url: https://www.crazyforcrust.com/easy-white-bread/
servings: 24
yield: 2%loaves
time: 1h50m
---

> **Yeast** — Use instant yeast, not active dry. RapidRise is one brand. Check the date on the packet.

Combine the @all-purpose flour{248%g}(2 cups), @granulated sugar{37%g}(3 tbsp), @instant yeast{14%g}(2 packets, 4 1/2 tsp), and @salt{2%tsp} in the bowl of a #stand mixer{} and stir until blended.

Combine the @water{1 1/2%cup}(355 ml), @milk{1/2%cup}(118 ml), and @butter{28%g}(2 tbsp, at room temperature) in a #microwave-safe bowl{}. Microwave on high in 15-second bursts until an #instant-read thermometer{} reads 120 to 130°F (49 to 54°C), very warm but not hot to the touch. The butter won't melt completely. Pour into the flour mixture.

> **Swaps** — Use the same amount of honey in place of the sugar. Any milk works, dairy or not. Oil, coconut oil, or margarine can replace the butter.

Beat with the dough hook at medium speed for ~beat{2%minutes}, scraping the bowl now and then. Add the @&all-purpose flour{124%g} (1 cup) and beat at high speed for ~beat{2%minutes} more.

Stir in the remaining @&all-purpose flour{372%g} (3 cups) a little at a time, until the dough forms a ball and pulls away from the sides of the bowl.

> **By Hand** — Skip the mixer. Stir the warm liquid into the dry ingredients in a large bowl with a wooden spoon until you can't stir anymore, then turn the shaggy dough out and knead.

Knead on a lightly floured surface until the dough is smooth and springs back when pressed lightly with 2 fingers, ~knead{6-8%minutes}. Cover with a #towel{} and let rest for ~rest{10%minutes}.

Cut the dough into 2 equal pieces. With a #rolling pin{}, roll each piece into a 12-by-7-inch rectangle.

Starting at a short end, roll each rectangle up tightly. Pinch the seam and ends to seal. Coat two #loaf pans{}(8 1/2 by 4 1/2 inches) with nonstick cooking spray and set a loaf in each, seam side down.

Cover with the towel and let rise in a warm place until doubled in size, about ~rise{45%minutes}. Meanwhile, heat the oven to 400°F (200°C) with a rack in the center.

Bake until the loaves are golden brown and 190°F (88°C) in the center, ~bake{20-30%minutes}. Run a knife around the edge of each pan and turn the loaves out onto a #wire rack{} to cool.

> **Storing** — Keeps on the counter for 2 to 3 days. To freeze a loaf, let it cool completely, then wrap it in plastic wrap.
